{%- set faqs = [
  ["What is IoT security testing?", "IoT security testing is a structured assessment of connected devices and the systems around them: the hardware, firmware, wireless and network communications, mobile apps and cloud services. Testers look for weaknesses that could let an attacker take control of a device, steal data or use it as a way into your network."],
  ["What is OT security?", "Operational technology (OT) security protects the systems that monitor and control physical processes, such as programmable logic controllers (PLCs), SCADA systems, human-machine interfaces and building management systems. Because these systems affect safety and production, the priority is availability and safe operation, not only confidentiality."],
  ["How is OT security different from IT security?", "IT systems usually prioritize confidentiality, while OT systems prioritize safety and availability. OT equipment often runs for decades, cannot be patched or rebooted easily and speaks industrial protocols that were designed without security. Testing and fixes therefore have to be planned carefully around operations."],
  ["Is it safe to security test industrial systems?", "It can be, when it is planned for safety. We begin with passive discovery and documentation review, use lab replicas or staging equipment wherever possible, agree testing windows and stop conditions with your operations team, and avoid actions that could disrupt a live process. Active tests on production equipment are only done where agreed in advance."],
  ["Do you test production environments?", "Only where you have agreed to it and the risk is understood. Most of the work can be done on documentation, network captures, configuration reviews, lab devices and test environments. Where production testing adds value, we limit it to safe, read-only checks under your supervision."],
  ["What is an ICS or SCADA security assessment?", "An ICS or SCADA security assessment reviews industrial control systems for weaknesses in architecture, network segmentation, remote access, device configuration, protocols and access control. It shows how an attacker could move from a corporate network toward process control systems, and what to change to prevent it."],
  ["What is IEC 62443?", "IEC 62443 is a series of international standards for the cybersecurity of industrial automation and control systems. It defines security levels, zones and conduits, and requirements for asset owners, system integrators and product suppliers. Our reporting can map findings to it."],
  ["What is firmware analysis?", "Firmware analysis examines the software that runs on a device. We extract and inspect it for hard-coded credentials, insecure update mechanisms, outdated components with known vulnerabilities, debug interfaces and weak cryptography. It often reveals issues that cannot be seen from the network alone."],
  ["What is the difference between IT/OT segmentation review and a penetration test?", "A segmentation review examines how your networks are separated, checking firewall rules, remote access paths and shared services against your design. A penetration test goes further and attempts to cross those boundaries. We can do either, or combine them, depending on your goals and risk appetite."],
  ["Can you test medical devices, smart buildings and robotics?", "Yes. We assess medical and healthcare devices, building management and access control systems, warehouse and logistics automation, and robotic systems. Each has its own protocols, safety considerations and regulatory context, and we adapt the approach to suit."],
  ["How long does IoT and OT security testing take?", "Duration depends on the number of device types, the size of the network and the depth of testing. A single device assessment can be completed in a short engagement, while a plant-wide OT assessment takes longer and needs careful scheduling. We confirm the timeline after scoping."],
  ["How much does IoT and OT security testing cost?", "Cost depends on the number and complexity of devices and systems in scope, the depth of testing and the reporting required. Share a short description of your environment with CipherTrivia and we will recommend a scope and quote."],
  ["What does the report include?", "The report includes an executive summary, an inventory of the assets tested, each finding with its severity, steps to reproduce, evidence and affected component, and a recommended fix. Where relevant, findings are mapped to IEC 62443 and related guidance, with fixes that account for operational constraints."],
  ["Do you offer retesting after fixes are made?", "Yes. Retesting can be included to confirm that reported weaknesses have been addressed and that changes have not disrupted operations or opened new gaps. The retest results are added to the report."]
] %}

