<section class="section section--white" aria-labelledby="s1-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="split__aside">
        <h2 class="split__title rv" id="s1-title">IoT and OT Security Testing for Connected Devices and Industrial Systems</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="split__body prose">
        <p class="rv">Internet of Things (IoT) devices and operational technology (OT) now sit in factories, hospitals, warehouses, buildings and customers' homes. Many were designed for reliability, not for attackers, and they often run for decades on firmware that is hard to update. When they are compromised the consequences go beyond data: production stops, services fail and physical safety can be at risk.</p>
        <p class="rv">CipherTrivia's IoT and OT security testing examines the whole chain: the device hardware and firmware, the wireless and industrial protocols it speaks, the network zones that separate it from the office, and the mobile apps and cloud services that manage it. We show how an attacker could get in, move and affect operations.</p>
        <p class="rv">Safety comes first. We plan every engagement with your operations team, start with passive discovery, use lab equipment where possible and agree testing windows and stop conditions. The result is a set of prioritized fixes that account for uptime, maintenance windows and the realities of the plant floor.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

