<section class="section section--white" id="risks" aria-labelledby="s3-title">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="shead">
      <div class="shead__meta"></div>
      <div class="shead__body">
        <h2 class="shead__title rv" id="s3-title">IoT and OT Security Risks We Look For</h2>
        <p class="shead__lede rv" style="--d:1">The same weaknesses appear again and again in connected and industrial systems. Our testing is built to find them, and to show how they combine into real attack paths.</p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="ledger ledger--10">
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("key") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Default and Hard-Coded Credentials</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Factory passwords and embedded keys that are shared across devices and easy to find.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:1">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("update") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Outdated and Unpatched Firmware</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Known vulnerabilities in components that cannot be easily updated.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:2">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("cloud-alert") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Insecure Update Mechanisms</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Updates that are not signed or verified, letting an attacker install their own code.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("globe") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Exposed Services and Remote Access</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Devices and vendor connections reachable from the internet or from other networks.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:1">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("segments") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Weak IT/OT Segmentation</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Firewall rules and shared services that let an attacker move from the office to the plant.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:2">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("unlock") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Insecure Industrial Protocols</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Protocols with no authentication, so anyone on the network can read or issue commands.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("eye-off") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Unencrypted Communications</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Traffic that can be read or altered on the wire or over the air.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:1">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("terminal") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Exposed Debug and Physical Interfaces</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Serial and debug ports that give direct access to firmware and memory.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv" style="--d:2">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("api") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Insecure Cloud and Mobile Backends</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Management apps and APIs that expose or control every device from one weakness.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="ledger__cell rv">
        <div class="ledger__head">{{ icon("dependency") }}</div>
        <h3 class="ledger__title">Supply Chain and Third-Party Components</h3>
        <p class="ledger__text">Vulnerable libraries, vendor tools and integrator accounts that sit outside your control.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

