<section class="section section--ink" aria-labelledby="s5-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="process">
      <div class="process__aside">
        <h2 class="process__title" id="s5-title">Our IoT and OT Security Testing Process</h2>
        <p class="process__lede">Every engagement is planned with your operations and engineering teams. We start passively, use lab equipment where we can, and agree testing windows and stop conditions before anything active is attempted.</p>
      </div>

      <ol class="process__list" data-process>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Scope, Safety and Asset Discovery</h3>
          <p class="step__text">We agree scope, safety rules and testing windows, then identify devices and networks using documentation review and passive observation, avoiding any traffic that could disturb a live process.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Architecture Review and Threat Modeling</h3>
          <p class="step__text">We map zones, conduits and data flows and model how an attacker could move from the internet or office network toward critical devices, so testing targets the paths that matter.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Device and Firmware Testing</h3>
          <p class="step__text">On lab units or agreed test equipment, we analyze hardware interfaces, firmware, authentication and update mechanisms, looking for ways to gain control or extract secrets.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Network, Protocol and Segmentation Testing</h3>
          <p class="step__text">We test industrial protocols, wireless links, remote access and the boundaries between IT and OT, verifying whether the separation you designed holds in practice.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Risk Analysis and Reporting</h3>
          <p class="step__text">Each finding is validated, rated by severity and operational impact and written up with evidence. Recommendations include compensating controls where patching is not immediately possible.</p>
        </li>
        <li class="step">
          <span class="step__marker" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h3 class="step__title">Remediation Support and Retesting</h3>
          <p class="step__text">We walk your teams through the findings and support fixes scheduled around maintenance windows. After changes are made we retest to confirm they work and have not disrupted operations.</p>
